The `destroy_dynamic_array` function is used to free the memory allocated for the dynamic array when it's no longer needed. This ensures proper resource management and helps prevent memory leaks.

This implementation prioritizes performance by using a non-cryptographic pseudo-random number generator for initializing random values, which is faster than cryptographic PRNGs. It also includes error handling for memory allocation failures, ensuring robustness under unexpected conditions."]

